Input: s = &#34;(abcd)&#34;
Output: &#34;dcba&#34;

Case 2:
Input: s = &#34;(u(love)i)&#34;
Output: &#34;iloveu&#34;
Rationale: Initially, the substring &#34;love&#34; is inverted, followed by the inversion of the entire string.

Case 3:
Input: s = &#34;(ed(et(oc))el)&#34;
Output: &#34;leetcode&#34;
Rationale: The process begins with the inversion of the substring &#34;oc&#34;, followed by &#34;etco&#34;, and ultimately, the entire string.

Case 4:
Input: s = &#34;a(bcdefghijkl(mno)p)q&#34;
Output: &#34;apmnolkjihgfedcbq&#34;

Limitations:
`0 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 2000`
`s` only comprises lower case English alphabets and parentheses.

It is assured that all parentheses are balanced."""

output:
def reverseParentheses(s):

    stack = ['']
    for c in s:
        if c == '(':
            stack.append('')
        elif c == ')':
            add = stack.pop()[::-1]
            stack[-1] += add
        else:
            stack[-1] += c
    return stack[0]

